ped me Khan anyway yeah I got  it there we go but anyway share your  three points in an instructive format  it's very effective the tenth strategy I  want to share with you is work harder  than your opponent very simple campaigns  are hard work they involve writing a  campaign plan and recruiting volunteers  raising money you know making your  direct mail pieces going door-to-door  meeting people getting out to vote on  Election Day all those things that are  in my book kind of try to lay it all out  and very easy to understand format so  you can just take your one resource and  put together a campaign but it's  work but I wanted to let you know even  though it's an arduous task it can be  fun too and very rewarding fun and that  you get to meet people you never would  have met before going door to door most  people are very appreciative of people  willing to put their name on the line  and file for office they appreciate that  and they'll be glad to hear why you run  they may not end up voting for you but  they'll respect you for doing it  especially if you do it an honorable way  with integrity and it's rewarding  because you get to have input into  things you care about  and have a say in those things so it is  very important that we have good people  in office and I hope that you will  consider using your gifts and talents  and use those things take the stands  that need to be taken and and be that  future generation of leaders that we  need and I just wanted to close with a  verse that I found when I was in junior  high that minute has meant a lot to me  and I think he has a lot to say about  not just life but campaigns holds true  because it talks about how you can have  favor with man with God talks about  reputation talks about how you can have  success so I just wanted to share it  with you is proverbs 3 verses 4 through  6 in the living bible version and it  says if you want favor with God and man  and a reputation for good judgment and  common sense then 